WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.001
FAREED ZAKARIA: The World
Economic Forum in Davos

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.970
is usually fixated
on the future.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:08.274
Most years, the attendees
are dazzled by some country,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:13.479
company, or technology promising
to burst forward, force change,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.849
dominate the next decade.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:19.819
This year, the focus was not
on the future, but the past.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:23.289
People delve back into
history to debate what caused

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.257
Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.093 line:8%
The Swedish finance
minister explained

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.161 line:8%
why his country,
which hasn't been

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.630 line:8%
at war since the
Napoleonic wars,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:35.034 line:8%
was breaking its 200-year
tradition of neutrality

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.836 line:14%
with his bid to join NATO.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.273
The Finnish foreign minister
recalled Finland's resistance

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:46.278
to Moscow's aggression in the
Winter War of 1939 and 1940.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.782
In past years at Davos,
companies took storefronts

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.585
and plastered them
with jubilant signs,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:57.022
cheering on dynamism,
acceleration, and disruption.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.359 line:8%
This time, there were far
fewer placards and slogans,

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:03.095 line:8%
some of them meekly
promising sustainability

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.531 line:14%
or progress on climate change.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.834 line:8%
The one genuinely
cheerful sign I saw

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.637 line:8%
said, "Will the Saudi
GDP now be fueled

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:16.308 line:14%
by YOLO, FOMO, and WYWH?"

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.278
With oil at over $100 a
barrel, the Saudi regime

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.948
has much to be excited about.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.284
The storefront that
dominated detention

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.787
was one that used to be booked
for years by Russians who

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.122
hosted lavish cocktail
parties and caviar

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.992
tastings there with the
country's moneyed elite.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:37.997
Now, it has a sign in the window
that reads in small cleartype

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:41.167
"This used to be the
Russian house in Davos.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:45.437
Now, it's the Russian war
crimes house in Davos."

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.341
Sponsored by the Ukrainian
businessman Viktor Pinchuk,

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.177
the rooms are filled
with striking images

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.080
and stories of Russia's
barbaric actions

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.248
in its campaign against Ukraine.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.717
Ukraine dominated
Davos this year,

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.619
and most people I
spoke to were quite

00:02:00.652 --> 00:02:03.188
unsure how this war would end.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.625
That played into a larger sense
of uncertainty about the world

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.294
that we are heading into.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.830
A world of multiplying risks.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.866
Tharman Shanmugaratnam,
Singapore's senior minister,

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:18.537
said to me, "We know the risks
that are out there are large.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:22.074
They're not about black swan
events, coming out of the blue.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.110
A pandemic was predicted.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.213
Russia's invasion was
a known possibility.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.516
Another pandemic or more
frequent climate crises--

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.052
these are not just
possible, but likely.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:36.489
We can't keep expecting
and planning for a return

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.392
to calm, untroubled times."

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.127
A former central
banker told me that

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.429
economic policymakers
felt that they

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.199
were in uncharted territory.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.168
"The old model-- where inflation
moves up ever so slightly,

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:52.238
and then you raised rates a tiny
bit and all was well-- that's

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.573
dead.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:57.476
We're in a new world, and
we're all just experimenting."

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:01.080
There is a broader foreboding, a
sense that the era we have just

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.450
lived through, the three
decades since 1990,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:07.553
may have been an unusual,
perhaps, even unique

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:10.289
one in which great
power politics

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.959
and geopolitical tensions that
normally dominate and define

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.329
international life were absent.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.432
The giddy trends
of recent times--

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.101
globalization, the
information revolution,

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.804
even democratization--
were trends

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:30.442
built on an edifice of power,
America's superpower status.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.977
But that strength
has been waning

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:36.048
for some years, caused by Iraq,
the global financial crisis,

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.116
COVID.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.218
Now, it is being
challenged-- first

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.288
by China, and then Russia.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.525
In all this gloom, there's
one distinctly hopeful sign.

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:49.162
Europe is acting with a greater
sense of unity and purpose

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.863
than I've ever seen before.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.965
Every European
leader I spoke with

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.468
believe that Russia's aggression
has sparked a revolution

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.537
of sorts across the continent.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.807
The EU has shown remarkable
unity on sanctions,

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.809
and is slowly but
steadily coming

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.945
together on energy policy.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.147
These successes could
evolve into greater

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:11.617
coordination on foreign,
and even defense policy.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:14.453
Europeans have realized
at a fundamental level

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.923
that they were taking peace
and stability for granted.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:21.194
That it might now have to
be created and sustained

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.796
by hard work and
commitment, in part,

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.732
by building hard power of
their own and deploying

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.100
it strategically.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.169 line:8%
There are serious
debates about ending

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.773 line:8%
the slow, consensual process
of EU decision making

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:38.110 line:8%
that allows one country like
Hungary to veto its efforts.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.146
The most lasting
legacy of this crisis

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:43.148
could be a new role
for Europe as a more

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:46.518
purposeful, strategic
actor on the world stage.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:50.389
But for that to happen,
this experience in uniting

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.259
against Russia has to work.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:56.362
Only success can
breed more success.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.565
Failure will doom
this experiment.

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:02.034
The founding fathers
of the European Union,

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.671
like Robert Schuman and Jean
Monnet, were steeped in history

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:08.107
and determined to
ensure that war did

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.376
not break out again in Europe.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:14.179
Today's statesmen need to infuse
their day to day decisions

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.815
with a similar sense of history.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:20.753
50 years from now, no one will
remember whether growth slowed

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:24.590
on the continent for a
couple of quarters in 2022

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:28.695
or if Brussels had to pay extra
for natural gas from the US.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:33.165
What they will recall is
the answer to one question.

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.701
Who won the war in Ukraine?

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:38.537
Putin or the West.

